R3216 closeout evidence - a same-name rewrite of evidence is now announced.

WHAT CHANGED (one door, one line)
  tools/qa_log.py do_write reads the target it is about to replace, before the
  replace, and prints one line after the write:
    QA-LOG REPLACED name=<n> old_bytes=<b> old_sha16=<h> new_bytes=<b> new_sha16=<h>
  Fresh names print nothing. Identical-bytes rewrites print the line too, with
  old_sha16 == new_sha16, so "nothing changed" is visible and not assumed.
  write_atomic is untouched: the law lives at the evidence door only.

WHY (measured, read-only first)
  tmp/probe_R3216.py and tmp/probe_R3216b.py, private temp worlds, zero socket,
  zero network, zero write to the live qa/ tree; report at
  tmp/probe-R3216-report.txt, landed as qa/probe-R3216.log.
  (a) decisive arms: writing the same name twice with different bodies answered
      rc=0 both times, printed only the second sha16, and read back clean both
      times; the census answered class=tee for the first version and the second,
      so the replaced evidence survived nowhere on disk.
  (b) cost of a refusal: git history holds 117 modify events over 75 qa/ paths,
      of which 72 events over 69 *.log paths - re-landing is an established
      workflow (the R3212 suite log alone has carried at least two bodies under
      one name), so refusing would have blocked it. The announcement is the
      option that costs zero and hides nothing.
  (c) call sites: 22 do_write calls in the tree, 3 of them round-named literals,
      and 58 --from invocations on shipped surfaces across 2 files.

CRITERIA (pinned in src/os/backlog.md before any code was written)
  AC-QALB24 the replaced identity is named: fresh name zero lines, rewrite
           exactly one line with the measured old and new bytes and sha16,
           identical rewrite prints old == new.
  AC-QALB25 the file itself is unchanged: landed bytes equal the normalized
           payload, no .tmp survives, dialect utf-8/lf, and do_check answers the
           same OK shape with the same three fields (it never gains the word).
  AC-QALB26 the law is scoped: the line exists at exactly one string literal in
           the tool, write_atomic never announces, a direct write_atomic call
           still lands silently, and the live qa/ tree is stable.

GATES
  SUITE PASS 28/28 over 26 criteria (qa/suite-qa-log-R3216.log, written and
  re-read through the shipped writer); qa_log --selftest VERDICT PASS 9/9 with
  the real qa/ untouched; os-battery-shard SUITE PASS 32/32; os-evidence-read
  17/17; os-suite-output-audit 6/6; suites matrix regenerated through its own
